concept.details:
Instead of a static +60dB global amp hack, the new implementation (ALC269_FIXUP_VAIO_EAPD_5DB) uses a firmware fixup offset mapping at 0x14.
This offset is tied specifically to the Sony VAIO vendor ID (SND_PCI_QUIRK_VENDOR(0x104d, "Sony VAIO")).
By modifying the amp capability offset cleanly (using the 0x14 hex step offset, which is roughly +5.5dB balanced), it retains the ALSA slider linearity while boosting output pins, preventing the "Blast Zone" distortion.

Code implementation details:

static void alc269_fixup_vaio_eapd_5db(struct hda_codec *codec,
                                  const struct hda_fixup *fix, int action)
{
        u32 caps;
        if (action != HDA_FIXUP_ACT_PRE_PROBE)
                return;
        static hda_nid_t nids[] = { 0x14, 0x21 };
        int i;
        for (i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
                caps = query_amp_caps(codec, nids[i], HDA_OUTPUT);
                if (caps) {
                        // Modifying amp capability offset cleanly instead of hardcoding raw gain
                        snd_hda_override_amp_caps(codec, nids[i], HDA_OUTPUT,
                                                  (caps & ~AC_AMPCAP_OFFSET) |
                                                  (0x14 << AC_AMPCAP_OFFSET_SHIFT));
                }
        }
        codec_info(codec, "ALC269: VAIO EAPD (+5.5dB balanced offset) unleashed!\n");
}

Vendor mapping:
SND_PCI_QUIRK_VENDOR(0x104d, "Sony VAIO", ALC269_FIXUP_VAIO_EAPD_5DB),
